WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.516
For each alternative–scenario pair, assess how
well the design satisfies that scenario.

00:00:05.516 --> 00:00:11.348
Jeromy illustrates Poor, Fair, Good and
Excellent mapped to 0, 1, 2 and 3. Define
consistent

00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:16.800
anchors and record evidence. For a timing
target, Good might mean the agreed target is

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.541
demonstrated; other ratings need equally
explicit meanings.

00:00:20.541 --> 00:00:27.412
A prototype result, an analysis and an untested
assertion do not offer the same confidence.

00:00:27.412 --> 00:00:34.208
New hypothetical score matrix, ordered Search /
Export / Worker loss / New source: A = [3,

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:40.475
2, 1, 0]; B = [1, 2, 3, 3]. These ratings are
invented for the exercise and are not

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:42.664
assessments of real products.

00:00:42.664 --> 00:00:55.919
The total is Σ(scenario weight × rating). A =
0.4583×3 + 0.1528×2 + 0.2778×1 + 0.1111×0 ≈

00:00:55.919 --> 00:01:02.472
1.9583. B ≈ 1.9306, using unrounded weights.

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:07.596
A leads by only about 0.0278 on the 0–3 scale.
That small difference should prompt

00:01:07.596 --> 00:01:12.949
investigation of uncertain ratings rather than a
claim of scientific certainty. The model

00:01:12.949 --> 00:01:18.361
assumes the rating numbers can be used
additively; it makes tradeoffs inspectable but
does

00:01:18.361 --> 00:01:23.834
not establish objective utility. Missing
evidence is not the same as Poor. Leave an
unknown

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:27.743
visible and gather evidence before presenting a
complete ranking.

00:01:27.743 --> 00:01:32.420
Also test hard constraints separately: if Worker
loss must score at least Good, A is

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:37.430
ineligible in this example even though it has
the higher unconstrained weighted total. The

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:42.552
lecture deliberately uses four rating categories
with no neutral midpoint. The lab’s Unknown

00:01:42.552 --> 00:01:47.674
state is an added evidence-tracking safeguard,
not a fifth numeric rating in Jeromy’s scale.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:51.237
Gather evidence before replacing it with a
supported assessment.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:56.434
Alternative A has the largest weighted score but
fails a mandatory recovery requirement.

00:01:56.434 --> 00:02:01.624
Should it automatically win? No. Apply the
mandatory requirement as a feasibility check.

00:02:01.624 --> 00:02:06.873
Weighted scores support tradeoffs among eligible
choices; they do not override a declared

00:02:06.873 --> 00:02:07.817
hard constraint.

00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:13.665
Change an assumption deliberately and
recalculate. If Availability becomes first and

00:02:13.665 --> 00:02:19.862
Performance second, with Maintainability still
third, the top-level weights become 0.6111

00:02:19.862 --> 00:02:26.128
for Availability, 0.2778 for Performance and
0.1111 for Maintainability. Search and Export

00:02:26.128 --> 00:02:30.445
keep their local ordering but receive smaller
combined shares.

00:02:30.445 --> 00:02:36.186
Under that new ordering, the same score matrix
gives A ≈ 1.3750 and B ≈ 2.5139. The

00:02:36.186 --> 00:02:42.065
preferred alternative changes because
stakeholder priorities changed, not because the

00:02:42.065 --> 00:02:47.252
arithmetic was inconsistent. Explain that causal
chain in a recommendation.

00:02:47.445 --> 00:02:53.332
Also vary uncertain ratings. In the original
ordering, reducing A’s Search rating from 3 to

00:02:53.332 --> 00:02:59.218
2 lowers its total by about 0.4583, easily
reversing the narrow lead. This identifies where

00:02:59.218 --> 00:03:05.040
a prototype or benchmark may be valuable.
Sensitivity analysis asks whether the conclusion

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:10.020
survives plausible changes, not how to tune the
inputs until a favorite wins.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:15.469
The case emphasizes revisiting the framework
during planning cycles as business priorities

00:03:15.469 --> 00:03:20.977
and technologies change. Retain the scenarios,
rankings, evidence and rationale so the team

00:03:20.977 --> 00:03:26.304
can update the decision without reconstructing
every discussion. Add new alternatives or

00:03:26.304 --> 00:03:31.450
scenarios when justified. The ranking changes
after stakeholders prioritize recovery.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:36.653
Does that prove the method is broken? No. A
preference-sensitive method should respond to a

00:03:36.653 --> 00:03:41.560
real priority change. Report which assumption
changed and whether uncertainty makes the

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.858
recommendation fragile.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:48.389
Jeromy extends the same framework to technical
debt. A deliberate shortcut can buy delivery

00:03:48.389 --> 00:03:53.345
time by accepting lower quality in specific
scenarios. The time saved is the benefit

00:03:53.345 --> 00:03:58.595
obtained; the obligation is the gap between the
desired and actual quality of the system.

00:03:58.595 --> 00:04:03.712
Repayment effort need not equal the effort
initially saved. New example: a team ships a

00:04:03.712 --> 00:04:08.710
fixed-format importer in two weeks instead of
spending six weeks on a general adapter

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:14.121
framework. It gains four weeks now, but the
actual system performs poorly on a future “add a

00:04:14.121 --> 00:04:15.120
source” scenario.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:20.337
Later integrations, changed code and new
requirements may make closing that gap more or
less

00:04:20.337 --> 00:04:21.812
expensive than four weeks.

00:04:21.812 --> 00:04:26.721
Compare the actual design and a desired design
against the same current scenario tree.

00:04:26.721 --> 00:04:31.859
Inspect weighted per-scenario gaps to locate the
important deficiencies, then estimate the

00:04:31.859 --> 00:04:36.997
work and risk of addressing them. Do not confuse
a quality-score difference with engineer-

00:04:36.997 --> 00:04:41.792
days; the score helps prioritize investigation,
while the effort estimate comes from

00:04:41.792 --> 00:04:42.991
engineering analysis.

00:04:42.991 --> 00:04:48.599
The target can change over time. If new-source
integration becomes central to the business,

00:04:48.599 --> 00:04:54.083
its quality gap matters more. If the system is
retired, that particular investment may no

00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:59.444
longer have value. Document the shortcut,
affected scenarios, intended benefit, current

00:04:59.444 --> 00:05:04.867
consequences, and a review trigger. The lecture
does not establish a fixed interest-rate

00:05:04.867 --> 00:05:06.531
formula for technical debt.

00:05:06.531 --> 00:05:11.688
The team saved four weeks by taking a shortcut.
Does repayment necessarily require four

00:05:11.688 --> 00:05:16.963
weeks? No. What remains is a quality gap, and
the system and its requirements may change.

00:05:16.963 --> 00:05:22.060
Estimate the current effort to close the
relevant gap rather than equating it with the

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.305
original time saving.

00:05:23.531 --> 00:05:29.365
Your deliverable is a defensible decision
record: decision and context; stakeholders and

00:05:29.365 --> 00:05:35.199
hard constraints; quality tree; concrete
scenarios; sibling rankings and rationales; ROC

00:05:35.199 --> 00:05:40.966
calculations and path products; alternative-by-
scenario ratings with evidence; weighted

00:05:40.966 --> 00:05:45.408
comparison; sensitivity checks; recommendation
and review triggers.

00:05:45.531 --> 00:05:50.726
Use the interactive lab to reproduce the worked
example. First predict the winner, then

00:05:50.726 --> 00:05:55.742
calculate. Change the top-level order, test an
unknown rating, and activate the hard

00:05:55.742 --> 00:06:01.117
recovery constraint. For each change, write one
sentence explaining why the recommendation

00:06:01.117 --> 00:06:04.043
changes or why the comparison becomes
incomplete.

00:06:04.043 --> 00:06:09.886
Independent exercise: evaluate two notification
architectures for a campus safety service.

00:06:09.886 --> 00:06:15.729
Create your own contexts, stimuli and responses
for urgent delivery, failure behavior, and

00:06:15.729 --> 00:06:21.313
adding a new channel. Use at least one two-level
branch, compute ROC path weights, and

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:25.209
compare two alternatives using stated
hypothetical evidence.

00:06:25.209 --> 00:06:30.357
Do not reuse the Search/Export scores as if they
were measurements. Mastery means explaining

00:06:30.357 --> 00:06:35.450
the reasoning behind every cell. A correct
spreadsheet with vague scenarios, hidden missing

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:40.375
evidence or post-hoc priorities is not a sound
architectural evaluation. A strong answer

00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:45.468
makes disagreement visible and proposes the next
experiment that could change the decision.

00:06:45.709 --> 00:06:50.733
What should a reviewer be able to reconstruct
from your final score? The scenario

00:06:50.733 --> 00:06:56.441
definitions, tree paths, sibling rankings,
weight calculations, rating evidence,
constraints

00:06:56.441 --> 00:07:01.776
and sensitivity checks. A total without this
trail is not an adequate decision record.
